 "notes": "Hand-built on a 127.0 BPM grid fitted to the drum stem (residual 8 ms). Each bar pattern was chosen from per-bar 16-step onset maps of the demucs stems (kick/clap/bass/vocal/synth) and every tap is snapped to the nearest real onset of its tagged stem within 45 ms. Chorus = halftime kick/snare + the synth hook answering on the off-8ths (call-and-response); bridge = syncopated trap kick; dance break = four-on-the-floor 8th runs (8-tap and 10-tap runs).",
